Hamnix Micro feather-nrf52840 size patch to kernel/pipe.ad.
Applied by scripts/mkroot.sh in build/feather-nrf52840/root only; the
committed file is unchanged.

Reason: the nRF52840 has 256 KiB of RAM for everything: kernel data, kernel
stacks and heap, the files in / and every running program's stack and data
(boards/feather_nrf52840/link.ld; programs' code stays in flash).

    pipe buffer (kernel heap, per open pipe)   4 KiB -> 1 KiB
A four-stage pipeline holds three pipes.  A writer blocks when its pipe is
full, so the only effect is on vfork'd shell code that writes into a stage
not yet started (README, "rfork is vfork"): it may now write 1 KiB, not 4.

Only constants, array lengths, and messages that quote them change.
Generated by editing a copy and
    diff -u --label a/kernel/pipe.ad --label b/kernel/pipe.ad kernel/pipe.ad <copy>

--- a/kernel/pipe.ad
+++ b/kernel/pipe.ad
@@ -23,7 +23,7 @@
 from mm.slab import kmalloc, kfree
 
 PIPE_MAX: uint32 = 16
-PIPE_CAP: uint32 = 4096             # a power of two
+PIPE_CAP: uint32 = 1024             # a power of two (Hamnix Micro feather-nrf52840: was 4096)
 PIPE_COPY: uint32 = 1024            # bytes copied per critical section
 EPIPE: int32 = -32
 EAGAIN: int32 = -11
